+### Step 294 [token localization] — isolate and preregister local fusion optimization
+
+**What**: Created the isolated branch
+`codex/token-local-fusion-optimization-v1` and worktree
+`local_cache/worktrees/token_local_fusion_optimization_v1`. Added a design-only
+protocol for a common 29-stream token-fusion ladder: equal mean, equal-family
+mean, exact IU-PCR, fixed SU-PCR, STG-SU-PCR, DUFS-LIU, token-native continuous
+B3, and token-native CIW-B3. The global response head is fixed to equal-30 for
+the primary ablation so the experiment measures local fusion rather than two
+changes at once.
+
+**Why**: A read-only modern reconstruction on the eight Qwen ProcessBench
+cells found that equal-30 global + IU-local nearly reproduces IU/IU
+(`30.7052%` versus `30.8570%` macro F1), while equal-30 global + equal-29 local
+falls to `26.2942%`. The local-fusion loss is `-4.4110` F1 points with paired
+95% CI `[-5.8843,-2.9406]`; the global-head change is only `-0.1519` points,
+CI `[-0.6132,+0.3005]`. Token fusion, not response fusion, is therefore the
+specific optimization target.
+
+**Result**: The next-session research contract is documented at the design
+level and still requires an executable hash freeze before fitting. ProcessBench
+first-error localization is primary, PRMBench every-step ranking
+is a separate transfer panel, and detector/clean-abstention metrics remain
+separate from locator metrics. Targets may not select gates, supports,
+regularization, reducers, or blend strengths. This step ran no fit, opened no
+new label, created no score artifact, and makes no performance claim. Current
+populations remain retrospective; promotion requires a frozen score boundary
+and later confirmation on a new population.
