+### Step 296 [token localization] — test Unified-28 transform clustering and reject hierarchical compression
+
+**What**: Independently adapted the external Claude Token-Head Feature Atlas
+claim to the signed target-free localization release.  Reconstructed the seven
+linear Unified-28 base risks from prepared coordinates, replayed `level`,
+`ewma16`, `positive_area`, and `persistence`, and compared flat IU against a
+four-block transform hierarchy, a seven-block source hierarchy, and 20 fixed
+capacity-matched random partitions on 12 ProcessBench model-family cells.  The
+protocol, A/B freezes, source/environment closure, serialized models, and
+post-audit evaluator are hash-bound.
