+## Transform clustering — structural premise confirmed, hierarchy rejected (Step 296)
+
+The external Token-Head Feature Atlas identified a real descriptive property
+of Unified-28: causal coordinates cluster more strongly by transform than by
+source stream.  A separate target-free 12-cell diagnostic reproduces the
+ordering in every cell (`0.901102` mean absolute Spearman for same transform,
+`0.565975` for same source, `0.524352` for neither).  This refines the old
+response-level clustered U-PCR failure: the transform blocks exist, so the old
+conclusion should not be stated as "there is no cluster structure."
+
+The stronger algorithmic inference is rejected.  Compressing each transform
+block with IU and then fusing the four block scores loses `0.020542`
+ProcessBench macro F1 versus flat IU, with paired 95% CI
+`[-0.030048,-0.010891]` and only three of 12 cell wins/ties.  Transform
+hierarchy does beat source hierarchy and the fixed random-partition mean at the
+point estimate, so the partition is not arbitrary; the harmful step is the
+hierarchical scalar compression itself.  Equal-28 is slightly above flat IU
+but inconclusive because its paired interval reaches zero.  Therefore this
+finding does not reopen clustering or promote a new localizer.  A future
+mechanism would need to exploit block geometry without collapsing seven
+sources to one scalar, under a new frozen protocol and fresh population.
